      "question": "q-75829",
      "field": null,
      "attribute": "question/problem",
      "old_sha256": "e655cb69ae98cc387ed0d5eb7b7e631303793855448578182fc2c75560c67602",
      "new_sha256": "e2b106c13cbb4a6e25e6991c7b4eae0d85d19374f136ec8ae0a7067f1285f454",
      "category": "ma_capture",
      "authoring": [],
      "source": [
        {
          "question": "q-75829",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/problem",
          "value": "The following table gives the values of functions $f(x)$ and ${f}^{\u2032}(x)$ at some points. Find $({f}^{-1})^{\u2032}(3).$\n\n| **$x$** | $f(x)$ | ${f}^{\u2032}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $4$ | $-9$ | $0$ |\n| $5$ | $3$ | $-2$ |",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037063/state.json",
          "file_sha256": "2a45135769e9e6b2a2ae9e14439682f6ef0f9ab51ecd85f119a8f7079a4e1990"
        }
      ],
      "basis": 1253,
      "reason": "Observed MA content supersedes the stored value",
      "action": "replace",
      "transaction_receipt": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037063/edb-import/commit.edn",
      "basis_after": 1254
    },
    {
      "question": "q-75829",
      "field": null,
      "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
      "old_sha256": "1531451da1f6eb7edb41f56396ed0642f52d25d92eaf686907c5823991cdb1c1",
      "new_sha256": "2b8181edf3d15e08985cb3708e9ed2a23d468ae93f10802e8c4c80df735600e8",
      "category": "ma_capture",
      "authoring": [],
      "source": [
        {
          "question": "q-75829",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "The formula for the derivative of the inverse is\n\n$$\n({f}^{-1})^{\u2032}(x)=\\frac{1}{{f}^{\u2032}({f}^{-1}(x))}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=3,$ we have\n\n$$\n({f}^{-1})^{\u2032}(3)=\\frac{1}{{f}^{\u2032}({f}^{-1}(3))}.\n$$\n\nFrom the table, we obtain ${f}^{-1}(3)=5$ and ${f}^{\u2032}(5)=-2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({f}^{-1})^{\u2032}(3) & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{\u2032}({f}^{-1}(3))} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{\u2032}(5)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(-2)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037063/state.json",
          "file_sha256": "2a45135769e9e6b2a2ae9e14439682f6ef0f9ab51ecd85f119a8f7079a4e1990"
        }
      ],
      "basis": 1253,
